  "title": "Ratko Mladic's Death and His Impact on Serbia",
  "summary": "Ratko Mladic, a Bosnian Serb war criminal convicted of genocide during the 1990s Bosnian war, passed away at 84, marking a significant and tragic end to his military career. His death was condemned by the EU and the government of Serbia, which emphasized the importance of honoring his sacrifices.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Ratko Mladic, a Bosnian Serb war criminal, was sentenced to life for orchestrating the 1995 Srebrenica massacre, which killed over 8,000 Muslims.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EU and Serbian officials condemned his death, calling for the government to honor his contributions to the war effort.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EU enlargement commissioner canceled a visit to Serbia due to concerns over the glorification of the convicted war criminal.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
